## ⭐️ Two must‑do activities  

| # | Activity | Why it’s a highlight | Quick tips to enjoy it |
|---|----------|----------------------|------------------------|
| **1** | **Mount Royal Park (Parc du Mont‑Royal)** – “the heart of the city” | • Panoramic city views from the **Kornberg Tower**.<br>• Late‑November still shows a splash of autumn colour, and the northern slopes have groomed snow‑shoe/kids‑ski tracks.<br>• Free, spacious green space for a relaxed walk or a quick picnic. | • Take the **Côte‑Coulonge** or **Camillien‑Houde** trail up to the tower (≈ 20 min walk).<br>• Dress warmly (0‑5 °C at the summit) and bring a hat/gloves.<br>• If you want a short snow‑shoe experience, rent gear at the **Mount Royal Chalet** (on‑site shop). |
| **2** | **Old Montreal (Vieux‑Montréal) historic walking tour** | • Cobblestone streets, 17th‑century architecture, and a lively mix of boutiques, cafés, and museums.<br>• Highlights: **Notre‑Dame Basilica**, **Place Jacques‑Cartier**, **Bonsecours Market**, and the **Old Port**.<br>• Consistently 4.8 ★+ on TripAdvisor and Google. | • Join a **guided walking tour** (≈ 90 min) – many free‑walk options are offered by local guides and include stories about the city’s French‑Canadian heritage.<br>• After the tour, linger at a café on **Rue Saint‑Paul** for a hot chocolate or a classic poutine snack.<br>• All major sights are within a 10‑minute walk, so you can explore at your own pace afterward. |
| **Bonus (if you have extra time)** | **Space for Life – Biodome / Botanical Garden / Insectarium** | One of the world’s most acclaimed indoor‑ecosystem complexes (rainforest, polar, tropical habitats). Great for a rainy afternoon. | Purchase a **combined ticket** (≈ CAD 30) and spend 3‑4 hours exploring the three venues. It’s a short metro ride from downtown. |

---

## 🏨 Two highly‑reviewed hotels (1 room, 2 adults)

| # | Hotel | Neighborhood | Approx. price per night* (CAD) | Rating (out of 10) | Key amenities & why guests love it |
|---|-------|--------------|--------------------------------|--------------------|------------------------------------|
| **1** | **Maison Sainte‑Thérèse by Maisons & Co** | Old Montreal (≈ 1.1 km from the historic centre) | **≈ CAD 690** (USD ≈ 492 gross) | **9.1 – Superb** | • Private suite (38 m²) with 2 beds, living‑room area and a full bathroom.<br>• Stylish historic building with modern décor.<br>• Very high guest scores for cleanliness, location and staff friendliness.<br>• Walking distance to Notre‑Dame Basilica, Place Jacques‑Cartier and the Old Port. |
| **2** | **Hotel St. Thomas** | Downtown – city‑centre location | **≈ CAD 860** (USD ≈ 650 gross) | **8.7 – Fabulous** | • Classic hotel room with 1 bed, modern furnishings and free Wi‑Fi.<br>• Central spot (steps from the Bell Centre, underground city and metro lines).<br>• Guests praise the comfortable beds, helpful front‑desk staff and quiet rooms.<br>• Free cancellation up to 48 h before arrival. |
| **Alternative (if you prefer a boutique‑style stay)** | **Bakan – Palais des Congrès, Convention Centre** | Near the Convention Centre, city centre | **≈ CAD 580** (USD ≈ 430 gross) | **8.0 – Very good** | • Entire apartment (42 m²) with 1 bed, living area and kitchen.<br>• Good for couples who like a bit of extra space and the option to self‑cater.<br>• Positive reviews for location, size and value. |

